`testcase.py` calls `Faker.seed(seed)` immediately before constructing `Faker()` and invoking `password(...)`, so each parametrized case starts from the same PRNG state on every independent run. In `Provider.password`, the executed lines are determined by the four boolean-guarded `if` blocks, the always-executed assertion and initial password generation, and the `while` loop that keeps drawing indexes until enough unique ones are collected. Since all randomness comes from the seeded shared generator and the same arguments are supplied each time, the same random draws occur in the same order, which means the same branches are taken and the `while` loop iterates the same number of times for each case on every run. Therefore all 15 parametrized tests follow identical line-number sequences across all 10 executions.

